  <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,710.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.Y.M SHAFA</td>\n                <td>₦1,720.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,690.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ZAMSON</td>\n                <td>₦1,690.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,690.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>BULK STRATEGIC</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SAHARA</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Brent Surges Past $91 After Vessel Hit in Strait of Hormuz\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude climbed above $91 a barrel on Tuesday after a cargo vessel was struck by an unidentified projectile while transiting the Strait of Hormuz. The incident was reported by the United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations (UKMTO), a Royal Navy-sponsored maritime security organisation. The attack comes as tensions between the United States and Iran remain high.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/brent-surges-past-91-after-vessel-hit-in-strait-of-hormuz\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Refinery Adds Four More States to Free Petrol Delivery at ₦1,165/Litre\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Dangote Petroleum Refinery has added four more states to its free petrol delivery scheme. Kano, Imo, Anambra and Nasarawa now join Lagos, Ogun, Rivers, Kaduna, Abuja and Delta. Petrol under the scheme would sell for ₦1,165 per litre and marketers who qualify get ten days' credit before payment is due.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-refinery-adds-four-more-states-to-free-petrol-delivery-at-1165litre\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Petrol Landing Cost Hits ₦1,218/litre, Surpasses Dangote Gantry Price by 5%\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria's downstream market is seeing a widening gap between the cost of imported petroleum products and Dangote Petroleum Refinery’s domestic selling prices. The differential is increasingly influencing sourcing decisions among marketers and depot operators. The latest spot assessments show that petroleum product prices have strengthened significantly.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/petrol-landing-cost-hits-1218litre-surpasses-dangote-gantry-price-by-5\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Climb Nearly 3% After Iran Rules Out Strait of Hormuz MOU\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Oil prices rose sharply on Monday as Iran rejected an extension of its understanding with the United States. Brent crude was trading at $90.66 per barrel, up $2.14, or 2.42% , while West Texas Intermediate (WTI) stood at $84.27 per barrel. The rally came after Iran ruled out extending a memorandum of understanding reached with Washington in June.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-climb-nearly-3-after-iran-rules-out-strait-of-hormuz-mou\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Trump to Iran: Surrender or Face Military Strikes\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    US President Donald Trump has demanded that Iran surrender to end the war with the United States. Speaking to a Fox News reporter by phone on Monday, Trump said Iran should “put up the white flag of surrender” Comments came as an interim agreement between the United. States and Iran appeared to have collapsed.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/trump-to-iran-surrender-or-face-military-strikes\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
